Found by mcp-hub, the second consumer. In .github/dzil-binary/build-leg.sh verify() calls leg_env without lib, so PERL5LIB, PERL_LOCAL_LIB_ROOT, PERL_MB_OPT and PERL_MM_OPT are unset and the packing perl sees nothing from the leg's local lib; the local check in Binary.pm after_build runs the same hook with the caller's environment, PERL5LIB included. mcp-hub's verify compares each case against 'perl -Ilib bin/mcp-hub' and recomputes the packed module set with scripts/loaded-modules.pl; both need a perl that loads the dist's dependencies and die in the CI leg with Can't locate Mojo/Base.pm. mcp-wiki's verify needs only core modules.

Shape: the hooks get DZIL_BINARY_PERL5LIB, the PERL5LIB value under which the packing perl loads the dist's dependencies; PERL5LIB itself stays out of the hook's environment, so the binary under test never sees it. The same contract in the CI leg and in the local check. POD and the leg contract say so. mcp-wiki's scripts stay green.

